1
00:04:28,976 --> 00:04:30,846
You should consider yourself lucky.

2
00:04:33,026 --> 00:04:34,956
At least your balls won't freeze off.

3
00:04:35,056 --> 00:04:36,726
You take great offense at dwarf jokes,

4
00:04:36,736 --> 00:04:39,066
but love telling eunuch jokes. Why is that?

5
00:04:40,276 --> 00:04:42,936
Because I have balls, and you don't.

6
00:05:10,696 --> 00:05:11,666
I warned you.

7
00:05:12,386 --> 00:05:14,746
Northerners don't much trust outsiders.

8
00:06:36,666 --> 00:06:37,636
Look at you.

9
00:06:39,366 --> 00:06:40,396
You're a man.

10
00:06:41,496 --> 00:06:42,566
Almost.

11
00:07:02,436 --> 00:07:04,936
- Where's Arya? - Lurking somewhere.

12
00:07:11,986 --> 00:07:14,226
Queen Daenerys of House Targaryen.

13
00:07:15,576 --> 00:07:19,596
My sister, Sansa Stark, the Lady of Winterfell.

14
00:07:19,626 --> 00:07:22,146
Thank you for inviting us into your home, Lady Stark.

15
00:07:22,776 --> 00:07:25,506
The North is as beautiful as your brother claimed,

16
00:07:25,836 --> 00:07:26,666
as are you.

17
00:07:30,986 --> 00:07:33,066
Winterfell is yours, Your Grace.

18
00:07:34,806 --> 00:07:36,696
We don't have time for all this.

19
00:07:37,166 --> 00:07:40,326
The Night King has your dragon. He's one of them now.

20
00:07:41,386 --> 00:07:42,766
The Wall has fallen,

21
00:07:42,986 --> 00:07:44,696
the dead march south.

22
00:07:50,646 --> 00:07:52,436
As soon as we heard about the Wall,

23
00:07:52,436 --> 00:07:55,586
I called all our banners to retreat to Winterfell.

24
00:07:56,756 --> 00:07:57,826
Lord Umber...

25
00:07:59,356 --> 00:08:01,556
when can we expect your people to arrive?

26
00:08:06,346 --> 00:08:09,906
We need more horses and wagons, if it please my lady.

27
00:08:12,526 --> 00:08:14,306
And my lord.

28
00:08:16,476 --> 00:08:20,316
And my queen. Sorry.

29
00:08:20,326 --> 00:08:22,326
You'll have as many as we can spare.

30
00:08:22,526 --> 00:08:25,216
Hurry back to Last Hearth and bring your people here.

31
00:08:28,336 --> 00:08:30,726
We need to send ravens to the Night's Watch as well.

32
00:08:31,346 --> 00:08:33,126
There's no sense in manning the castles anymore.

33
00:08:33,126 --> 00:08:34,396
We make our stand here.

34
00:08:34,786 --> 00:08:36,086
At once, Your Grace.

35
00:08:36,956 --> 00:08:37,976
"Your Grace."

36
00:08:44,136 --> 00:08:46,156
But you're not. Are you?

37
00:08:46,966 --> 00:08:49,616
You left Winterfell a king and came back a--

38
00:08:52,476 --> 00:08:53,916
I'm not sure what you are now.

39
00:08:55,256 --> 00:08:56,106
A lord?

40
00:08:57,226 --> 00:08:58,456
Nothing at all?

41
00:08:59,826 --> 00:09:01,726
- It's not important. - Not important?

42
00:09:02,896 --> 00:09:05,296
We named you King in the North.

43
00:09:06,606 --> 00:09:08,596
King of the North!

44
00:09:13,236 --> 00:09:15,136
You did, my lady.

45
00:09:16,606 --> 00:09:18,176
It was the honor of my life.

46
00:09:18,816 --> 00:09:20,956
I'll always be grateful for your faith.

47
00:09:23,586 --> 00:09:24,616
But when I left Winterfell,

48
00:09:24,616 --> 00:09:27,536
I told you we need allies or we will die.

49
00:09:28,596 --> 00:09:30,576
I have brought those allies home

50
00:09:30,586 --> 00:09:32,386
to fight alongside us.

51
00:09:33,656 --> 00:09:34,966
I had a choice,

52
00:09:35,576 --> 00:09:38,906
keep my crown or protect the North.

53
00:09:39,516 --> 00:09:41,426
I chose the North.

54
00:09:53,856 --> 00:09:56,146
If anyone survives the war to come,

55
00:09:56,416 --> 00:09:58,166
we'll have Jon Snow to thank.

56
00:09:59,666 --> 00:10:02,276
He risked his life to show us the threat is real.

57
00:10:02,306 --> 00:10:03,796
Thanks to his courage,

58
00:10:03,896 --> 00:10:05,556
we have brought with us the greatest army

59
00:10:05,556 --> 00:10:06,876
the world has ever seen.

60
00:10:07,306 --> 00:10:10,426
We have brought two full-grown dragons.

61
00:10:12,496 --> 00:10:13,806
And soon, the Lannister army

62
00:10:13,806 --> 00:10:16,736
will ride north to join our cause.

63
00:10:20,606 --> 00:10:22,266
I know, I know, our people

64
00:10:22,266 --> 00:10:24,816
haven't been friends in the past.

65
00:10:27,166 --> 00:10:28,836
But we must fight together now...

66
00:10:29,876 --> 00:10:30,696
or die.

67
00:10:33,036 --> 00:10:35,716
May I ask, how are we meant to feed

68
00:10:35,716 --> 00:10:38,236
the greatest army the world has ever seen?

69
00:10:38,236 --> 00:10:40,286
While I ensured our stores would last through winter,

70
00:10:40,286 --> 00:10:42,266
I didn't account for Dothraki,

71
00:10:42,266 --> 00:10:45,716
Unsullied and two full-grown dragons.

72
00:10:47,516 --> 00:10:49,436
What do dragons eat, anyway?

73
00:10:51,476 --> 00:10:52,766
Whatever they want.

74
00:11:11,366 --> 00:11:15,286
Hey, careful, lads. We need every last bit of it.

75
00:11:15,286 --> 00:11:16,376
Sorry 'bout that.

76
00:11:21,156 --> 00:11:22,636
Are these the last of the wagons?

77
00:11:22,756 --> 00:11:23,556
Aye.

78
00:11:23,966 --> 00:11:26,286
All right, let's get it all to the forges.

79
00:11:34,696 --> 00:11:35,486
My lord.

80
00:11:37,746 --> 00:11:38,566
My lady.

81
00:11:45,296 --> 00:11:46,326
My lady.

82
00:11:58,316 --> 00:12:00,126
The Lady of Winterfell.

83
00:12:01,806 --> 00:12:03,156
Has a nice ring to it.

84
00:12:03,696 --> 00:12:05,276
So does Hand of the Queen.

85
00:12:07,006 --> 00:12:09,026
Depending on the queen, I suppose.

86
00:12:11,806 --> 00:12:14,006
Last time we spoke was at Joffrey's wedding.

87
00:12:15,746 --> 00:12:18,666
- Miserable affair. - It had its moments.

88
00:12:24,346 --> 00:12:26,406
Apologies for leaving like that.

89
00:12:26,406 --> 00:12:28,216
Yes, it was a bit hard to explain

90
00:12:28,216 --> 00:12:30,646
why my wife fled moments after the king's murder.

91
00:12:33,566 --> 00:12:34,836
We both survived.

92
00:12:37,606 --> 00:12:39,236
Many underestimated you.

93
00:12:40,626 --> 00:12:42,196
Most of them are dead now.

94
00:12:50,276 --> 00:12:51,936
I'm sure you weren't thrilled to hear

95
00:12:51,936 --> 00:12:53,886
the Lannister army's marching north.

96
00:12:56,216 --> 00:12:58,536
You have every right to be fearful of my sister.

97
00:12:59,646 --> 00:13:00,966
No one fears her more than I do.

98
00:13:00,966 --> 00:13:03,266
- But I promise, you'll be safe-- - Cersei told you her army

99
00:13:03,266 --> 00:13:06,236
was coming north to fight for you?

100
00:13:06,526 --> 00:13:07,276
She did.

101
00:13:09,136 --> 00:13:10,236
And you believed her?

102
00:13:12,026 --> 00:13:13,566
She has something to live for now.

103
00:13:14,386 --> 00:13:16,286
I believe she wants to survive.

104
00:13:19,326 --> 00:13:21,756
I used to think you were the cleverest man alive.

105
00:13:53,536 --> 00:13:54,876
You used to be taller.

106
00:13:58,036 --> 00:13:59,636
How did you sneak up on me?

107
00:13:59,776 --> 00:14:01,696
How did you survive a knife through the heart?

108
00:14:02,356 --> 00:14:03,096
I didn't.

109
00:14:22,396 --> 00:14:23,436
You still have it.

110
00:14:26,826 --> 00:14:27,546
Needle.

111
00:14:29,986 --> 00:14:31,316
Have you ever used it?

112
00:14:32,896 --> 00:14:33,866
Once or twice.

113
00:14:49,926 --> 00:14:51,106
Valyrian steel.

114
00:14:53,426 --> 00:14:54,176
Jealous?

115
00:14:55,796 --> 00:14:56,846
Too heavy for me.

116
00:15:05,676 --> 00:15:06,976
Where were you before?

117
00:15:07,956 --> 00:15:10,176
I could've used your help with Sansa.

118
00:15:12,556 --> 00:15:14,546
She doesn't like your queen, does she?

119
00:15:14,956 --> 00:15:17,426
Sansa thinks she's smarter than everyone.

120
00:15:18,986 --> 00:15:20,886
She's the smartest person I've ever met.

121
00:15:22,276 --> 00:15:23,506
Now you're defending her?

122
00:15:24,376 --> 00:15:25,106
You?

123
00:15:26,226 --> 00:15:27,706
I'm defending our family.

124
00:15:29,496 --> 00:15:30,386
So is she.

125
00:15:31,296 --> 00:15:32,016
Yeah.

126
00:15:33,686 --> 00:15:35,136
I'm her family too.

127
00:15:41,246 --> 00:15:42,426
Don't forget that.

128
00:16:00,436 --> 00:16:04,016
Your Grace, I'm afraid I bring terrible news.

129
00:16:04,946 --> 00:16:06,726
The dead have broken through the Wall.

130
00:16:10,386 --> 00:16:11,076
Good.

131
00:16:46,336 --> 00:16:48,556
Why don't you just get it over with and kill me?

132
00:16:50,246 --> 00:16:51,446
But we're family.

133
00:16:52,636 --> 00:16:55,386
The last Greyjoys left in the world.

134
00:16:58,256 --> 00:17:00,876
The last ones with balls anyway.

135
00:17:05,416 --> 00:17:06,946
If I kill you...

136
00:17:08,236 --> 00:17:09,726
who can I talk to?

137
00:17:14,656 --> 00:17:16,906
I've got a crew full of mutes.

138
00:17:20,206 --> 00:17:21,886
It gets lonely at sea.

139
00:17:24,726 --> 00:17:26,076
Are we in King's Landing?

140
00:17:32,556 --> 00:17:34,056
You picked the losing side.

141
00:17:38,176 --> 00:17:40,736
Then I'll sail the Iron Fleet somewhere else.

142
00:17:47,966 --> 00:17:50,836
But first I'm gonna fuck the queen.

143
00:18:04,486 --> 00:18:06,126
Twenty-thousand men, is it?

144
00:18:06,286 --> 00:18:09,356
Yes, Your Grace. A few died in transit.

145
00:18:11,476 --> 00:18:13,056
They cheated at dice.

146
00:18:14,906 --> 00:18:16,366
Or maybe I cheated.

147
00:18:17,036 --> 00:18:18,176
Someone cheated.

148
00:18:20,386 --> 00:18:22,636
They weren't good fighters. You won't miss them.

149
00:18:22,936 --> 00:18:24,716
- Horses? - Two thousand.

150
00:18:25,106 --> 00:18:26,256
And elephants?

151
00:18:26,256 --> 00:18:28,636
Uh, no elephants, Your Grace.

152
00:18:30,176 --> 00:18:31,396
That's disappointing.

153
00:18:32,766 --> 00:18:35,026
I was told the Golden Company had elephants.

154
00:18:35,036 --> 00:18:37,486
They are excellent beasts, Your Grace,

155
00:18:37,556 --> 00:18:40,646
but not well-suited to long sea voyages.

156
00:18:41,036 --> 00:18:42,606
In any event, you are most welcome

157
00:18:42,606 --> 00:18:44,846
here in King's Landing, Captain Strickland.

158
00:18:45,076 --> 00:18:48,176
We look forward to fighting on your behalf, Your Grace.

159
00:18:59,106 --> 00:19:00,796
Am I most welcome here?

160
00:19:02,316 --> 00:19:04,376
You are a true friend of the crown

161
00:19:05,466 --> 00:19:06,776
and an honored guest.

162
00:19:06,846 --> 00:19:07,546
Good.

163
00:19:08,516 --> 00:19:11,396
As a true friend and an honored guest...

164
00:19:20,306 --> 00:19:23,376
I was hoping we could talk in private.

165
00:19:24,376 --> 00:19:26,806
After the war. That was our agreement.

166
00:19:27,576 --> 00:19:30,556
Wars sometimes last years.

167
00:19:31,806 --> 00:19:33,556
You want a whore, buy one.

168
00:19:35,986 --> 00:19:37,216
You want a queen...

169
00:19:38,646 --> 00:19:39,646
earn her.

170
00:19:43,156 --> 00:19:43,876
How?

171
00:19:45,426 --> 00:19:46,746
I've given her justice,

172
00:19:46,746 --> 00:19:49,466
an army and the Iron Fleet,

173
00:19:49,666 --> 00:19:52,576
yet she gives me no sign of affection.

174
00:19:53,576 --> 00:19:55,806
My heart is nearly broken.

175
00:19:58,006 --> 00:19:59,386
You're insolent.

176
00:20:01,296 --> 00:20:03,416
I've executed men for less.

177
00:20:03,416 --> 00:20:04,966
They were lesser men.

178
00:20:44,886 --> 00:20:47,386
I hear the dragon burnt up a thousand Lannister men.

179
00:20:47,386 --> 00:20:49,206
Burnt up some of my favorite boys.

180
00:20:49,206 --> 00:20:51,026
- Archie, was it? - And William.

181
00:20:51,026 --> 00:20:54,496
- Tall handsome William? - Yeah, tall handsome William.

182
00:20:54,506 --> 00:20:56,736
They said what's left of him could fit in a wine glass.

183
00:20:56,736 --> 00:21:00,056
I am the only man you ever met who shot a dragon.

184
00:21:00,506 --> 00:21:02,256
- Did you? - Nearly killed it.

185
00:21:02,256 --> 00:21:03,456
That's brave.

186
00:21:13,476 --> 00:21:16,196
- That boy Eddie... - The ginger?

187
00:21:16,316 --> 00:21:19,346
That's him. Came back with his face burnt right off.

188
00:21:19,396 --> 00:21:20,936
He's got no eyelids now.

189
00:21:20,936 --> 00:21:22,406
How does he sleep with no eyelids?

190
00:21:22,406 --> 00:21:24,716
All right, can we stop talking about the fucking dragons now?

191
00:21:24,716 --> 00:21:26,436
Ser Bronn of the Blackwater.

192
00:21:29,156 --> 00:21:30,266
You're kidding me.

193
00:21:30,476 --> 00:21:31,616
Apologies for the interruption,

194
00:21:31,616 --> 00:21:33,456
but the queen did urge me to hurry.

195
00:21:36,456 --> 00:21:37,656
Sorry, ladies.

196
00:21:39,626 --> 00:21:41,306
Another time perhaps.

197
00:21:49,126 --> 00:21:52,436
You ever get lonely, I am partial to older gentlemen.

198
00:21:55,866 --> 00:21:59,196
Poor girl. The pox will take her within the year.

199
00:22:01,276 --> 00:22:01,946
Which girl?

200
00:22:01,956 --> 00:22:04,856
The queen's brothers made promises to you and broke them.

201
00:22:05,616 --> 00:22:07,906
Her Grace wants to rectify their mistake.

202
00:22:09,466 --> 00:22:11,986
She once gave me a castle and a wife,

203
00:22:12,026 --> 00:22:13,796
then rectified me right out of them.

204
00:22:13,796 --> 00:22:15,686
That was Ser Jaime's doing, not hers.

205
00:22:16,266 --> 00:22:17,946
When Queen Cersei wants something,

206
00:22:17,946 --> 00:22:19,966
she pays in advance and in gold.

207
00:22:19,966 --> 00:22:21,626
Several chests of it, in fact.

208
00:22:21,836 --> 00:22:24,736
Waiting for you in a wagon just outside.

209
00:22:29,676 --> 00:22:33,726
So she wants to murder someone, but she can't send her soldiers.

210
00:22:34,696 --> 00:22:36,616
If it's the Dragon Queen she's after...

211
00:22:36,626 --> 00:22:38,926
She has other plans for the Targaryen girl.

212
00:22:39,466 --> 00:22:40,986
Yeah, well, good luck with that.

213
00:22:41,076 --> 00:22:42,816
Our queen's brothers are unlikely

214
00:22:42,816 --> 00:22:45,286
to survive their Northern adventures.

215
00:22:45,306 --> 00:22:47,876
But in the event that they do...

216
00:22:54,096 --> 00:22:57,816
She has a keen sense of poetic justice.

217
00:22:59,066 --> 00:23:00,666
That fucking family.

218
00:23:01,326 --> 00:23:02,626
When the Citadel expelled me,

219
00:23:02,626 --> 00:23:04,876
I thought I would die poor and alone,

220
00:23:05,036 --> 00:23:08,916
but in exchange for my service, Queen Cersei made me her Hand.

221
00:23:09,356 --> 00:23:10,726
What would she do for the man

222
00:23:10,726 --> 00:23:13,036
who rids her of her treasonous brothers?

223
00:23:29,846 --> 00:23:31,626
I wanted those elephants.

224
00:23:37,576 --> 00:23:38,556
So...

225
00:23:40,446 --> 00:23:44,536
how do I compare to the fat king?

226
00:23:45,556 --> 00:23:47,266
You're insulting my late husband?

227
00:23:47,316 --> 00:23:48,726
Are you offended?

228
00:23:53,306 --> 00:23:55,376
Robert had a different whore every night,

229
00:23:56,456 --> 00:23:58,656
but he still didn't know his way around a woman's body.

230
00:23:59,956 --> 00:24:01,296
And the Kingslayer?

231
00:24:06,816 --> 00:24:08,966
You enjoy risking your neck, don't you?

232
00:24:10,486 --> 00:24:11,686
Life is boring.

233
00:24:11,836 --> 00:24:14,796
You're not boring, I'll give you that.

234
00:24:26,616 --> 00:24:28,676
Do I please the queen?

235
00:24:30,166 --> 00:24:33,616
You might be the most arrogant man I've ever met.

236
00:24:35,716 --> 00:24:36,726
I like that.

237
00:24:39,586 --> 00:24:40,996
But now I want to be alone.

238
00:24:47,966 --> 00:24:50,666
I'm going to put a prince in your belly.

239
00:26:25,186 --> 00:26:27,386
Euron can't defend the Iron Islands,

240
00:26:27,916 --> 00:26:30,846
not if he's in King's Landing with all his men and his ships.

241
00:26:32,356 --> 00:26:33,796
We can take our home back.

242
00:26:34,806 --> 00:26:36,036
Daenerys went north.

243
00:26:36,036 --> 00:26:37,436
Daenerys will need somewhere to retreat

244
00:26:37,436 --> 00:26:38,936
if they can't hold the North.

245
00:26:39,916 --> 00:26:41,396
Somewhere the dead can't go.

246
00:26:47,396 --> 00:26:50,756
You're my queen. I go where you command.

247
00:26:55,656 --> 00:26:57,186
You want to go to Winterfell.

248
00:26:57,646 --> 00:26:59,006
To fight for the Starks.

249
00:27:02,886 --> 00:27:03,946
Go.

250
00:27:08,716 --> 00:27:10,466
What is dead may never die.

251
00:27:14,486 --> 00:27:15,896
What is dead may never die.

252
00:27:21,266 --> 00:27:22,966
But kill the bastards anyway.

253
00:27:51,236 --> 00:27:52,866
Welcome back, my lady.

254
00:27:53,646 --> 00:27:54,616
If you'd follow me...

255
00:27:55,426 --> 00:27:56,666
The Karstarks.

256
00:27:57,516 --> 00:27:58,816
One of the better sigils.

257
00:28:00,126 --> 00:28:01,606
Beats an onion, anyway.

258
00:28:03,136 --> 00:28:04,206
Can't argue with that.

259
00:28:05,036 --> 00:28:07,026
Not so long ago, the Starks and the Karstarks

260
00:28:07,026 --> 00:28:09,156
were slaughtering each other on the battlefield.

261
00:28:09,156 --> 00:28:11,416
Jon Snow brought peace to the houses.

262
00:28:11,416 --> 00:28:12,766
And our queen is grateful.

263
00:28:13,556 --> 00:28:15,906
Her gratitude is lovely, but that's not my point.

264
00:28:17,136 --> 00:28:19,786
The Northmen are loyal to Jon Snow, not to her.

265
00:28:20,086 --> 00:28:21,066
They don't know her.

266
00:28:21,066 --> 00:28:23,076
The Free Folk don't know her.

267
00:28:23,646 --> 00:28:25,986
I've been up here a while, and I'm telling you,

268
00:28:26,386 --> 00:28:27,726
they're stubborn as goats.

269
00:28:28,466 --> 00:28:31,156
You want their loyalty, you have to earn it.

270
00:28:42,566 --> 00:28:44,756
I sense that you're leading to a proposal.

271
00:28:46,066 --> 00:28:48,216
A proposal is what I'm proposing.

272
00:28:48,956 --> 00:28:51,646
On the off chance that we survive the Night King,

273
00:28:52,286 --> 00:28:53,796
what if the Seven Kingdoms,

274
00:28:53,796 --> 00:28:56,226
for once in their whole shit history,

275
00:28:56,486 --> 00:28:59,826
were ruled by a just woman and an honorable man?

276
00:29:02,416 --> 00:29:04,286
They do make a handsome couple.

277
00:29:04,306 --> 00:29:06,326
You overestimate our influence.

278
00:29:06,426 --> 00:29:09,356
Jon and Daenerys don't want to listen to lonely old men.

279
00:29:09,356 --> 00:29:10,516
I'm not that old.

280
00:29:12,516 --> 00:29:13,996
Not as old as him.

281
00:29:15,966 --> 00:29:18,126
Our queen respects the wisdom of age.

282
00:29:18,136 --> 00:29:19,416
Of course she does.

283
00:29:19,736 --> 00:29:22,436
Respect is how the young keep us at a distance,

284
00:29:22,596 --> 00:29:25,216
so we don't remind them of an unpleasant truth.

285
00:29:26,126 --> 00:29:27,236
What is that?

286
00:29:28,326 --> 00:29:29,806
Nothing lasts.

287
00:29:38,866 --> 00:29:40,466
Your sister doesn't like me.

288
00:29:45,786 --> 00:29:47,056
She doesn't know you.

289
00:29:49,396 --> 00:29:50,386
If it makes you feel any better,

290
00:29:50,386 --> 00:29:52,546
she didn't like me either when we were growing up.

291
00:29:52,576 --> 00:29:54,416
She doesn't need to be my friend...

292
00:29:55,966 --> 00:29:57,476
but I am her queen.

293
00:30:01,506 --> 00:30:03,116
If she can't respect me...

294
00:30:22,526 --> 00:30:23,446
What's the matter?

295
00:30:23,766 --> 00:30:25,266
The dragons are barely eating.

296
00:30:43,516 --> 00:30:44,496
What's wrong with them?

297
00:30:45,106 --> 00:30:46,396
They don't like the North.

298
00:31:02,696 --> 00:31:03,536
Go on.

299
00:31:09,926 --> 00:31:11,626
I don't know how to ride a dragon.

300
00:31:12,636 --> 00:31:14,846
Nobody does. Until they ride a dragon.

301
00:31:17,386 --> 00:31:18,996
What if he doesn't want me to?

302
00:31:19,776 --> 00:31:21,866
Then I've enjoyed your company, Jon Snow.

303
00:31:41,406 --> 00:31:42,986
What do I hold onto?

304
00:31:44,466 --> 00:31:45,566
Whatever you can.

305
00:33:42,396 --> 00:33:44,656
You've completely ruined horses for me.

306
00:33:53,966 --> 00:33:55,776
We could stay a thousand years...

307
00:33:57,976 --> 00:33:59,186
no one would find us.

308
00:34:01,906 --> 00:34:03,156
We'd be pretty old.

309
00:34:11,406 --> 00:34:13,356
It's cold up here for a southern girl.

310
00:34:14,536 --> 00:34:16,146
So keep your queen warm.

311
00:34:30,816 --> 00:34:32,126
Don't be afraid.

312
00:34:45,356 --> 00:34:46,436
That's good.

313
00:34:55,836 --> 00:34:57,536
- Gendry? - He's here.

314
00:35:03,876 --> 00:35:06,416
It isn't easy making a blade that big with dragonglass.

315
00:35:08,846 --> 00:35:11,256
You're saying you're good, is that it?

316
00:35:11,416 --> 00:35:12,606
I'm just saying it's a tricky material to--

317
00:35:12,616 --> 00:35:15,106
You know who makes weapons for the wildlings?

318
00:35:16,286 --> 00:35:17,816
Cripples and cocksuckers.

319
00:35:18,836 --> 00:35:21,296
- Which one are you? - Leave him be.

320
00:35:28,446 --> 00:35:29,856
I heard you were here.

321
00:35:32,646 --> 00:35:34,326
You left me to die.

322
00:35:35,246 --> 00:35:36,376
First I robbed you.

323
00:35:48,416 --> 00:35:50,696
You're a cold little bitch, aren't you?

324
00:35:54,336 --> 00:35:56,076
Guess that's why you're still alive.

325
00:36:04,216 --> 00:36:05,926
That was a nice ax you made for him.

326
00:36:06,846 --> 00:36:07,906
You've gotten better.

327
00:36:08,106 --> 00:36:10,246
Yeah, thanks. So have you.

328
00:36:11,746 --> 00:36:13,966
I mean, you look good.

329
00:36:15,486 --> 00:36:17,486
Thanks. So do you.

330
00:36:21,116 --> 00:36:23,526
It's not a bad place to grow up, if it wasn't so cold.

331
00:36:25,526 --> 00:36:27,246
Stay close to that forge, then.

332
00:36:27,306 --> 00:36:30,886
- Is that a command, Lady Stark? - Don't call me that.

333
00:36:31,376 --> 00:36:33,016
As you wish, milady.

334
00:36:40,086 --> 00:36:41,356
Here's my wish.

335
00:36:43,796 --> 00:36:45,026
Can you make it?

336
00:36:45,266 --> 00:36:46,826
What do you need something like this for?

337
00:36:47,416 --> 00:36:48,716
Can you make it or not?

338
00:36:48,756 --> 00:36:51,746
You already have a sword. What's that?

339
00:36:58,196 --> 00:36:59,386
It's Valyrian steel.

340
00:36:59,686 --> 00:37:01,586
I always knew you were just another rich girl.

341
00:37:04,396 --> 00:37:06,376
You don't know any other rich girls.

342
00:37:16,886 --> 00:37:17,686
Come in.

343
00:37:25,596 --> 00:37:27,526
Lord Glover wishes us good fortune,

344
00:37:27,526 --> 00:37:30,396
but he's staying in Deepwood Motte with his men.

345
00:37:33,256 --> 00:37:35,396
"House Glover will stand behind House Stark

346
00:37:35,396 --> 00:37:37,516
as we have for a thousand years."

347
00:37:39,206 --> 00:37:40,446
Isn't that what he said?

348
00:37:40,536 --> 00:37:43,076
"I will stand behind Jon Snow," He said.

349
00:37:44,916 --> 00:37:46,416
"The King in the North."

350
00:37:47,886 --> 00:37:49,416
I told you we needed allies.

351
00:37:49,416 --> 00:37:52,206
You didn't tell me you were going to abandon your crown.

352
00:37:52,476 --> 00:37:54,216
I never wanted a crown.

353
00:37:54,836 --> 00:37:57,106
All I wanted was to protect the North.

354
00:37:57,686 --> 00:38:00,286
I brought two armies home with me, two dragons.

355
00:38:00,286 --> 00:38:02,366
And a Targaryen queen.

356
00:38:03,296 --> 00:38:05,846
Do you think we can beat the Army of the Dead without her?

357
00:38:06,296 --> 00:38:08,976
I fought them, Sansa. Twice.

358
00:38:09,196 --> 00:38:10,946
You want to worry about who holds what title,

359
00:38:10,956 --> 00:38:12,986
I'm telling you it doesn't matter.

360
00:38:14,066 --> 00:38:16,216
Without her, we don't stand a chance.

361
00:38:25,466 --> 00:38:27,236
Do you have any faith in me at all?

362
00:38:29,486 --> 00:38:30,666
You know I do.

363
00:38:35,266 --> 00:38:36,566
She'll be a good queen.

364
00:38:37,946 --> 00:38:38,926
For all of us.

365
00:38:40,706 --> 00:38:41,976
She's not her father.

366
00:38:48,766 --> 00:38:50,266
No, she's much prettier.

367
00:38:56,016 --> 00:38:58,186
Did you bend the knee to save the North

368
00:38:58,706 --> 00:39:00,046
or because you love her?

369
00:39:28,706 --> 00:39:29,796
So you're the man?

370
00:39:31,606 --> 00:39:33,816
Which man am I, Your Grace?

371
00:39:34,176 --> 00:39:36,716
The one who saved Ser Jorah when no one else could.

372
00:39:37,076 --> 00:39:39,386
They could, they just wouldn't.

373
00:39:41,426 --> 00:39:44,536
I'll have to make some changes in the Citadel when I take my throne.

374
00:39:44,846 --> 00:39:47,146
A great service merits a great reward.

375
00:39:47,146 --> 00:39:49,966
Oh, it's my honor to serve you, Your Grace.

376
00:39:50,186 --> 00:39:52,246
Well, there must be something I could give you.

377
00:39:54,326 --> 00:39:56,096
If it's not too much trouble,

378
00:39:56,976 --> 00:39:58,666
I could use a pardon.

379
00:39:59,496 --> 00:40:00,496
For what crime?

380
00:40:02,066 --> 00:40:05,186
I borrowed a few books from the Citadel.

381
00:40:07,176 --> 00:40:09,156
And also a sword.

382
00:40:09,376 --> 00:40:11,896
- From the Citadel? - From my family.

383
00:40:13,416 --> 00:40:15,566
It's been in House Tarly for generations.

384
00:40:15,566 --> 00:40:17,606
It would've been mine anyway, eventually,

385
00:40:18,456 --> 00:40:21,406
but my father had other ideas.

386
00:40:23,716 --> 00:40:25,166
Not Randyll Tarly?

387
00:40:27,046 --> 00:40:28,056
You know him?

388
00:40:32,536 --> 00:40:35,086
I offered to let him retain his lands and titles

389
00:40:35,086 --> 00:40:36,326
if he bent the knee.

390
00:40:39,426 --> 00:40:40,476
He refused.

391
00:40:50,356 --> 00:40:51,166
Well...

392
00:40:53,806 --> 00:40:55,416
At least I'll be allowed home again,

393
00:40:55,926 --> 00:40:57,456
now that my brother's the lord.

394
00:41:01,456 --> 00:41:03,736
Your brother stood with your father.

395
00:41:20,866 --> 00:41:22,396
Thank you, Your Grace.

396
00:41:22,826 --> 00:41:23,926
For telling me.

397
00:41:24,326 --> 00:41:25,246
And m--

398
00:41:25,696 --> 00:41:28,916
- May I...? - Of course.

399
00:42:12,296 --> 00:42:13,626
What are you doing out here?

400
00:42:14,666 --> 00:42:16,496
Waiting, for an old friend.

401
00:42:18,416 --> 00:42:20,386
It's time to tell Jon the truth.

402
00:42:21,326 --> 00:42:22,456
No, no.

403
00:42:23,586 --> 00:42:26,426
You're his brother. Shouldn't you tell him?

404
00:42:27,346 --> 00:42:28,696
I'm not his brother.

405
00:42:29,746 --> 00:42:31,606
He trusts you more than anyone.

406
00:42:33,006 --> 00:42:34,206
Now's the time.

407
00:43:10,076 --> 00:43:11,006
Sam?

408
00:43:11,726 --> 00:43:14,766
I'm sorry, I know I'm not supposed to be down here.

409
00:43:18,836 --> 00:43:21,146
- Were you hiding from me? - Of course not.

410
00:43:22,256 --> 00:43:23,756
What are you doing in Winterfell?

411
00:43:24,466 --> 00:43:26,836
Or did you read every book in the Citadel already?

412
00:43:30,396 --> 00:43:31,396
What's wrong?

413
00:43:32,336 --> 00:43:33,966
Gilly? Is she all right?

414
00:43:33,966 --> 00:43:35,866
- She's good. - Little Sam?

415
00:43:37,746 --> 00:43:38,726
Don't you know?

416
00:43:40,216 --> 00:43:41,166
Know what?

417
00:43:42,706 --> 00:43:43,716
Daenerys...

418
00:43:44,846 --> 00:43:46,966
she executed my father and brother.

419
00:43:48,096 --> 00:43:49,356
They were her prisoners.

420
00:43:53,656 --> 00:43:54,936
She didn't tell you.

421
00:44:04,126 --> 00:44:05,246
I'm so sorry.

422
00:44:08,886 --> 00:44:10,496
We need to end this war.

423
00:44:12,336 --> 00:44:13,436
Would you have done it?

424
00:44:16,296 --> 00:44:18,076
Well, I've executed men who disobeyed me.

425
00:44:18,076 --> 00:44:19,766
You've also spared men.

426
00:44:20,406 --> 00:44:22,716
Thousands of wildlings when they refused to kneel.

427
00:44:22,716 --> 00:44:23,826
I wasn't a king.

428
00:44:26,226 --> 00:44:27,306
But you were.

429
00:44:29,146 --> 00:44:30,446
You've always been.

430
00:44:32,326 --> 00:44:33,976
I gave up my crown, Sam.

431
00:44:35,246 --> 00:44:35,966
I bent the knee.

432
00:44:35,966 --> 00:44:37,726
I'm not King in the North anymore.

433
00:44:37,726 --> 00:44:39,216
I'm not talking about the King in the North.

434
00:44:39,226 --> 00:44:41,706
I'm talking about the King of the bloody Seven Kingdoms.

435
00:44:50,156 --> 00:44:51,646
Bran and I worked it out.

436
00:44:51,906 --> 00:44:54,156
I had a High Septon's diary. Bran had...

437
00:44:55,806 --> 00:44:57,196
whatever Bran has.

438
00:44:57,336 --> 00:44:58,576
What are you talking about?

439
00:45:02,336 --> 00:45:03,386
Your mother...

440
00:45:04,516 --> 00:45:05,956
was Lyanna Stark.

441
00:45:07,466 --> 00:45:08,636
And your father...

442
00:45:10,116 --> 00:45:11,546
your real father

443
00:45:12,166 --> 00:45:13,766
was Rhaegar Targaryen.

444
00:45:15,966 --> 00:45:17,656
You've never been a bastard.

445
00:45:18,876 --> 00:45:22,116
You're Aegon Targaryen, true heir to the Iron Throne.

446
00:45:26,796 --> 00:45:29,276
I'm sorry, I know it's a lot to take in.

447
00:45:38,976 --> 00:45:42,476
My father was the most honorable man I ever met.

448
00:45:45,866 --> 00:45:47,936
You're saying he lied to me all my life.

449
00:45:48,086 --> 00:45:49,036
No.

450
00:45:49,956 --> 00:45:53,636
Your father-- Well, Ned Stark.

451
00:45:54,006 --> 00:45:56,806
He promised your mother he'd always protect you.

452
00:45:57,066 --> 00:45:59,646
And he did. Robert would have murdered you if he knew.

453
00:46:01,746 --> 00:46:03,026
You're the true king.

454
00:46:04,316 --> 00:46:06,356
Aegon Targaryen, Sixth of His Name,

455
00:46:06,356 --> 00:46:08,126
Protector of the Realm, all of it.

456
00:46:22,976 --> 00:46:25,236
- Daenerys is our queen. - She shouldn't be.

457
00:46:27,816 --> 00:46:29,816
- That's treason. - It's the truth.

458
00:46:31,566 --> 00:46:33,676
You gave up your crown to save your people.

459
00:46:35,636 --> 00:46:36,956
Would she do the same?

460
00:48:45,536 --> 00:48:47,316
Stay back, he's got blue eyes!

461
00:48:47,316 --> 00:48:49,196
I've always had blue eyes!

462
00:48:58,896 --> 00:49:00,116
Did you find anyone?

463
00:49:33,616 --> 00:49:34,846
The Umber boy.

464
00:49:35,826 --> 00:49:36,936
It's a message.

465
00:49:38,036 --> 00:49:39,256
From the Night King.

466
00:49:39,936 --> 00:49:43,586
His army's between us and Winterfell. We're on foot.

467
00:49:43,586 --> 00:49:45,596
We rode down from Castle Black.

468
00:49:45,876 --> 00:49:47,456
We can double up on the horses.

469
00:49:47,856 --> 00:49:51,356
If the horses last, we'll get there before the dead.

470
00:49:52,146 --> 00:49:54,346
We just have to hope the Night King doesn't come first.

471
00:50:46,426 --> 00:50:48,706
Keep moving! Straight up!

472
00:50:50,776 --> 00:50:53,566
Stay together! Don't fall behind!

